            <ArticleTitle>[A female with expiratory wheezing and inspiratory stridor].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>D1889</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 42-year-old woman was seen with an inspiratory stridor and expiratory wheezing. The wheezing responded quickly to asthma treatment. The stridor, however, was caused by a significant narrowing of the trachea between the branching of a tracheal bronchus ('bronchus suis' or ' pig bronchus') and the main carina.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
